# FAkka.Proc.Supervisor win5 dependency alignment

## Pre-work plan

- Background: ProcSupervisor RFC-PROC-0021 raises the active exact package from win4 to win5.
- Goal: keep the DevKit Server active consumer on the same exact package and prove Release compilation.
- Scope: Server package reference, this log and DevLog only; no DevKit behavior or deployment changes.
- Assumption: win5 is API-compatible with the win4 surface consumed by the Server; Release compilation is the dependency gate.
- Acceptance: Release build exits 0 with no compiler errors; existing dependency warnings remain out of scope.
- Risk: consumer restore could resolve an older package cache or expose a compile-time API break; use exact range and no-cache restore.

## Operations

- 2026-09-23: changed `FSharp.MCP.DevKit.Server.fsproj` from exact win4 to exact win5.
- 2026-09-23: Release build passed with 0 errors; existing NU1510/NU1608/NU1701 and low-severity NU1901 warnings remain unchanged in category.
